  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Training on strategic water management for governmental institutions in Peru (Part I)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims overall to strengthen the capacity of the governmental water institutions in Peru for implementing a long-term strategic water management approach in Peru and through a long-term partnership between the Netherlands and Peru (Blue Deal).This project will benefit the Peruvian community by using safer, environmentally friendly and efficient water management, guaranteeing a better water supply. Implementation of integrated watershed management can prevent flooding of populated areas. Peru has had a history of natural disasters resulting from the El Ni&#xf1;o weather phenomenon. In 2017, a massive flood hit the northern region of Peru, a highly vulnerable area. Peruvian authorities have since been working on an Integrated Water Resource Management plan.The Netherlands is in a great position to offer technical and institutional support to Peru. That will help in building capacity and creating a more sustainable plan for water management, which will be more resilient. The relevant counterparts from Peru and the Netherlands will hold exploratory talks at Expo Agua 2018, the largest water fair in Peru.The Blue Deal is a new programme of the Dutch Water boards and the Ministries of Foreign Affairs and Infrastructure and Water. The goal is to help 20 million people in forty basins to have access to clean, sufficient and safe water worldwide.</narrative>
  </description>
